# Kitty session for the `teardown` scratchpad (Super+D, files/gui/hypr/hyprland.lua).
#
# Two tabs in one window rather than a split: btop keeps the full pane width and
# the live kernel log is one ctrl+right away (files/kitty/key.conf:
# ctrl+left / ctrl+right switch tabs). Tab 1 is active on open.
#
# Started as `kitty-glass --class teardown --session ~/.config/kitty/teardown.session`
# from `hyprscratch teardown ...`: the class stays `teardown`, which is what both
# the daemon and the teardown-scratchpad window rule (float + size + move) match.
#
# `launch` runs the command directly, without a shell, hence the explicit
# `sh -c` for the pipe. `sudo dmesg` needs no password: modules/security/default.nix
# carries the narrow NOPASSWD entry for dmesg.
new_tab btop
launch btop
new_tab dmesg
launch sh -c "sudo dmesg -w | lazytail"
